course: dictionary
lesson: 596
title: Aviary: a home for birds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An aviary is a place where birds are kept. You can work out what it means from the words around it. «A walk-through aviary is a huge netted house where birds fly free over your head while you walk along the paths.» Huge, netted house and birds fly free are the clues. So an aviary is a big place where birds can fly about.
explain: Look at the rest of the sentence too: «...and two sets of doors stop anyone flying out.» The doors show that the birds are kept inside and cannot escape. An aviary is enclosed, which means shut in on all sides.
explain: Now check your meaning by swapping it in. «A walk-through aviary is a huge netted house where birds fly free over your head.» If you put in "a huge cage where birds fly free", the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: An aviary is a large cage, building or enclosed space where birds are kept.
fact: An aviary is big enough for birds to fly about in.
fact: A «walk-through aviary» lets visitors walk among the birds, as in zoos and bird parks.
fact: A «garden aviary» is often a small one, where a family keeps budgies or finches.
fact: Bird keepers use aviaries to care for birds, and sometimes to help rare birds breed.
exercise: «A walk-through aviary is a huge netted house where birds fly free over your head.» What is an aviary? | *A large cage, building or enclosed space where birds are kept | A big pond for fish | A bird's egg | Tall tree where birds build their nests
exercise: Ella's family keeps budgies in a «garden aviary». What is the aviary for? | To store the garden tools | *To keep the budgies in a space big enough to fly | To grow vegetables | To keep the rain out of the house
exercise: Which phrase means you can walk among the birds inside? | Garden aviary | Enclosed space | *Walk-through aviary | Small aviary
test: Why might scientists use an aviary for rare birds? | To keep the birds out of the wild for ever | To sell the birds as pets | *To help the rare birds breed in a safe, cared-for space | To make the birds louder
test: Which word is closest in meaning to aviary? | Puddle | *Enclosure | Kitchen | Meadow
exam: Jayden says «aviary» means a kind of small brown bird, like a robin. Is he right? | No, it is a kind of tree | Yes, it is a type of parrot | Yes, it is a small brown bird | *No, an aviary is a place where birds are kept
